(P) PARITY: #lonely rotations is EVEN at every odd prime (radius r=floor(p/n)):
   AP            : all even & iota-paired;  lonely: []
   GW            : all even & iota-paired;  lonely: []
   swap11(+22)   : all even & iota-paired;  lonely: ['p=41(r=2):#2', 'p=53(r=3):#2']
   swap13(+26)   : all even & iota-paired;  lonely: ['p=41(r=2):#2']

(WITNESS = iota-pair) the (n+q)-witness hole is the pair {+1,-1} mod (n+q):
   q=11: D=n+q=25, a=q^-1=16; uncovered radius-1 residues (the iota-pair) = [1] -> [1, 24]
   q=13: D=n+q=27, a=q^-1=25; uncovered radius-1 residues (the iota-pair) = [1] -> [1, 26]

(LEVER) 'within-1 suffices': AP is zero-lonely EVERYWHERE; a single swap opens an EVEN hole
   (>=2, an iota-pair), never exactly 1 -- so a danger-count reaching p-2 (all but one) => full
   coverage by parity. Max #lonely a single swap opens (the pair count) at n=14:
   swap11(+22)   : max #lonely = 2 at (41, 2) (even: True)
   swap13(+26)   : max #lonely = 2 at (41, 2) (even: True)
   GW            : max #lonely = 0 at None (even: True)
